Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `xs`, which this function consumes
  --> Tests/UI/view_return_consumed_owner.jet:1:44
    |
  1 | owned_head: fn(xs: &&[U8]) -> View<U8> { xs[0..<1] }
    |                                            ^^^^^^^
 Why: The `&&` parameter `xs` moves the value into this function, which frees it when it returns, so a returned window into it would outlive its owner
 Fix: Take `xs` as a read or `&` parameter so the caller keeps owning it, or return an owned copy with `.copy()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
